long.en:
Self Service Deploy is a single GLPI plugin that:

- stores tokens (SHA-256 only) in its own tables: glpi_plugin_selfservicedeploy_tokens,
  _logs (audit) and _locks (parallel-restart guard);
- serves GET /plugins/selfservicedeploy/front/restart.php?token=<t> — a page with the
  computer name and a "Zrestartuj usługę" button;
- on POST schedules the pre-configured deployinstall taskjob ("Restart MyService")
  for that single computer using the GLPI Inventory plugin classes
  (PluginGlpiinventoryTaskjobstate / PluginGlpiinventoryTaskjoblog);
- enforces CSRF (double-submit + Origin), rate limit (1 restart / computer / 2 min),
  parallel-restart lock, audit logging and readable errors;
- never accepts commands, service names, package ids or arbitrary code: everything
  is hardcoded in config.php and in the GLPI Inventory package.
